WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.623
At the end of the 19th century, the Boxers appeared in North China.

00:00:03.623 --> 00:00:06.955
Most of its members were peasants, with red cloth wrapped around their heads.

00:00:07.037 --> 00:00:10.323
They believed that practicing martial arts could protect their homes and villages.

00:00:10.323 --> 00:00:13.133
They opposed foreign forces entering China.

00:00:13.133 --> 00:00:16.904
Crowds carrying lanterns and banners gathered toward the cities.

00:00:16.904 --> 00:00:20.127
Peasants from villages along the way kept joining their ranks.

00:00:20.127 --> 00:00:24.096
In the year 1900, the situation suddenly escalated.

00:00:24.096 --> 00:00:27.662
An allied army made up of eight nations attacked and entered Beijing.

00:00:27.662 --> 00:00:31.348
Empress Dowager Cixi fled the capital with the emperor to take refuge.

00:00:31.348 --> 00:00:35.055
The common people of Beijing lived through days of chaos.

00:00:35.055 --> 00:00:37.982
A distant military camp appeared and disappeared in the morning mist.

00:00:39.076 --> 00:00:42.604
In 1901, the Qing court signed a treaty.

00:00:42.604 --> 00:00:45.413
The Boxer Protocol brought an enormous indemnity.

00:00:45.413 --> 00:00:49.057
The convoy traveled westward and disappeared into the dust.

00:00:49.057 --> 00:00:52.660
The Qing dynasty was burdened with a heavy indemnity obligation.

00:00:52.660 --> 00:00:55.428
This upheaval left the country even weaker.
